Pipeline Stages Detailed:

1. CHECKOUT Stage:
groovy
stage('checkout') {
    steps {
        git 'https://github.com/devopsbyraham/jenkins-java-project.git'
    }
}

- Clones the Java project from GitHub

2. BUILD Stage:
groovy
stage('build') {
    steps {
        sh 'mvn compile'
    }
}

- Compiles Java source code using Maven
- Creates `.class` files

3. TEST Stage:
groovy
stage('test') {
    steps {
        sh 'mvn test'
    }
}

- Runs unit tests
- Generates test reports

4. CODE QUALITY Stage (SonarQube Integration):
groovy
stage('code quality') {
    steps {
        sh '''
        mvn sonar:sonar \
          -Dsonar.projectKey=netflix \
          -Dsonar.host.url=http://13.38.32.159:9000 \
          -Dsonar.login=3f017506d83cd334fba02ecf9db706c429ab5d38
        '''
    }
}

Parameters Explained:
- `sonar.projectKey=netflix` → Unique identifier in SonarQube
- `sonar.host.url` → SonarQube server address
- `sonar.login` → Authentication token (generated in SonarQube UI)

5. ARTIFACT Stage:
groovy
stage('artifact') {
    steps {
        sh 'mvn clean package'
    }
}

- Creates final deployable artifact (JAR/WAR file)
- Cleans previous builds

